666228208,2026-10-10 19:10:38,TickerWorth,2026-10-10,0,0,,"$NVDA at $229.28 sits inside our range ($106.05 to $265.75, from 2 models), but only because the next two years are so strong. Guidance carries most of it: FY27 roughly +86%, FY28 ~+70%. Our model then lets growth fall to 10%, 5%, 3% with margins easing into the low 50s, and averages 30.4% a year over five years. Hold margins where they are and price alone asks for more than 25% a year. So the bear case isn&#39;t the next two years. It&#39;s whether the capex cycle has a down leg after FY28. Things that would show it: hyperscaler capex guides flattening, more chips bought with debt, and the memory-cost margin reset (gross margin guided to 71-72% in Q4). Not investment advice."
