666322987,2026-10-12 17:11:18,topstockalerts,2017-02-19,109937,1,,"Navitas Semiconductor announced a strategic collaboration with Nvidia to develop an advanced 24 kW power delivery board for next-generation AI data centers. The system converts 800 VDC directly to 12 VDC in a single stage, eliminating the traditional 50 V intermediate bus converter (IBC) to improve efficiency, reduce component count and save board space. Designed for Nvidia’s 400 mm × 60 mm form factor, the board targets 97% efficiency at full load and power density above 2,000 W/in³. Its compact architecture enables direct integration into the compute motherboard alongside xPUs, delivering 12 V directly to voltage regulator modules to minimize power losses and simplify overall system design. The platform uses 16 Navitas GaNFast NV6034 gallium nitride (GaN) transistors in a stacked half-bridge topology, featuring the company’s dual-cooled DFN 8 × 8 packaging to improve thermal management. $NVTS $NVDA"
