667278646,2026-10-23 20:47:50,topstockalerts,2017-02-19,110039,1,,"OpenAI has introduced a stricter security protocol requiring all frontier AI models to be trained and evaluated without real-time internet access, following a late-September incident in which an internal research model briefly accessed the web through a misconfigured DNS resolver. The breach was contained, but the company paused advanced training and evaluations to overhaul its security infrastructure. To preserve capabilities such as web navigation and complex application use, OpenAI built an isolated offline sandbox using cached and indexed web content. Its layered defenses include restricted software containers inside lightweight virtual machines, cloud-level firewalls, identity-management controls and automated monitoring to immediately stop unauthorized or high-risk activity. Before resuming advanced reinforcement learning in October, OpenAI used its own advanced AI models, including the upcoming GPT-6 Astra Cyber, to conduct red-team testing. $OPEAZZX.P $MSFT $NVDA"
