667316997,2026-10-25 16:09:21,CUPandHANDLE_CHARTS,2011-07-03,10799,2,,"$QQQ ~ Why does Uncle Elon Musk want to merge SpaceX and Tesla, in what would be the biggest merger in corporate history? Look past the rockets and the cars and you find two companies quietly turning into two halves of one AI machine, and once you see who owns which half, the merger stops looking like a deal Elon wants and starts looking like one he needs. The short answer is control. At Tesla every share carries one vote, so Elon held only about 13% of the votes, and he said he was uncomfortable growing Tesla into a leader in AI and robotics without about 25% voting control. At SpaceX, his ten-vote Class B shares give him more than 80% of the votes. So it was SpaceX, not Tesla, that bought xAl, the lab behind Grok and the Colossus supercomputer in Memphis. SpaceX now builds the brain: the computing power, the frontier models and Terafab, a planned Al chip factory in Texas. Tesla builds the body, the Optimus humanoid robot, and holds about 45 billion in cash. $TSLA $SPCX $SPY $NVDA"
